  // v0.15.5.3: Two-character SAPI fix on top of v0.15.5.2 BAT. v0.15.5.2 BAT showed the cursor input fix worked perfectly: log line 'sub_49FD50(2): pCurrentDialogSlot 0xFF -> 0x02' confirmed pCurrentDialogSlot was set, Aaron heard the cursor-move SFX when pressing arrows during the open dialog, opcode_ask returned 1, slot 2 trans 0->0x400->0x1000 with state 0->1->0xD, and the FieldDialog [ASK] hook fired in TWO BATs (Test #1 in doani1_2 spoke 'Selphie. "Wanna go up?". Selected: Go up. Stay'; Test #2 in doan1_2 spoke 'Battle. Battle' since that field's msg 0 is just the word 'Battle'). HOWEVER Aaron reported he heard only the mod's diagnostic announcement, NOT the dialog text. Diagnosis from the SAPI call sequence: the FieldDialog [ASK] hook fires DURING opcode_ask (after field_get_dialog_string returns the encoded text and set_window_object_ASK populates the slot, the engine's per-frame text path triggers our hook which calls ScreenReader::Speak(text, true)). Then opcode_ask returns and our Phase2_TestAsk's AnnouncePhase2Result calls ScreenReader::Speak("Dialog inject phase two A. Slot 2. Return code 1.", true) -- the second arg true means INTERRUPT in-flight speech. SAPI was halfway through speaking the dialog text when our diagnostic announcement preempted it. Aaron heard only 'Dialog inject phase two A...'. v0.15.5.3 fix: change ScreenReader::Speak's interrupt flag from true to false in BOTH AnnouncePhase1Result and AnnouncePhase2Result. This QUEUES the diagnostic announcement after the dialog text rather than cutting it off. Aaron will now hear: (1) the dialog text from the FieldDialog hook ('Selphie. \"Wanna go up?\". Selected: Go up. Stay'), then (2) the queued diagnostic announcement ('Dialog inject phase two A. Slot 2. Return code 1.'). Phase 1 gets the same fix proactively for consistency -- the v0.15.4 BAT had the same race but Aaron didn't notice (likely because Phase 1's MES dialog and the diagnostic announcement are textually similar enough). Other diagnostic Speak calls (error guards like 'Dialog inject opcode address missing' or 'Dialog inject crashed') still use interrupt=true intentionally -- those are error paths where preemption is correct. Two new comment blocks added explaining the rationale. Aaron also reported arrows moved Squall AND the dialog cursor SIMULTANEOUSLY -- this is a known limitation: our injected dialog doesn't suspend field input because we don't run the script-VM polling loop that normally blocks field movement during ASK. Phase 2b (chase wiring) will resolve this naturally since chase_ask_overlay already handles input gating during ASKs. Not addressed in v0.15.5.3. Files changed: src/dialog_inject.cpp (2 char changes + ~15 lines of new comment/rationale), src/ff8_accessibility.h (this version), CHANGELOG.md (top entry, push-quality body), DEVNOTES.md, NEXT_SESSION_PROMPT.md.
  // v0.15.5.2: Quick follow-up to v0.15.5.1 BAT. v0.15.5.1 BAT was a clean SUCCESS for Phase 2a's first press: Test #2 at 19:45:49 in doani1_2 saw opcode_ask return 1, gameObj.D2 acquire bit 2 (0x04), slot 2 transition advance 0 -> 0x400 -> 0x1000, state machine progress 0 -> 1 -> 0xD (ASK active with cursor), and the FieldDialog [ASK] hook fire on win[2] with 'Parsed 3 choices (firstQ=1 lastQ=3 curChoice=2)' speaking 'Selphie. "Wanna go up?". Selected: Go up. Stay'. Subsequent Shift+F12 presses correctly returned 5 (slot busy) since slot 2 was still locked. Empirical SWO_ASK arg map nailed: stack[SP-3]=arg2 -> slot+0x29 firstQ (got 1), stack[SP-2]=arg3 -> slot+0x2A lastQ (got 3), stack[SP-1]=arg4 -> slot+0x2C curQ (got 2, the cursor position; clamped to [firstQ, lastQ] by SWO_ASK's entry logic). Aaron didn't hear FF8's cursor-move SFX when pressing arrows during the open dialog because the .alloc branch we successfully reached does NOT call sub_49FD50; only the stage-1 setup path at 0x529683 does. Without sub_49FD50(slot), pCurrentDialogSlot (BYTE at 0x01D2B51C) is not pointing at our slot, so the engine's input handler doesn't send arrow keys to slot 2's curQ field. v0.15.5.2 fix: add sub_49FD50(slot) call before opcode_ask in Phase2_TestAsk. ~30 lines added (the call + pre/post pCurrentDialogSlot diagnostic logging + comment block). Hardcoded address 0x0049FD50 with __cdecl(int) signature, SEH-wrapped. Not promoted to FF8Addresses since sub_49FD50 is not in the JSM opcode dispatch table (no FFNx wrapping concern). Predicted v0.15.5.2 BAT outcome: clean save reload (slot 2 fresh), Shift+F12 press, opcode_ask returns 1 same as v0.15.5.1, dialog renders, but NOW pressing arrows moves the cursor and triggers FF8's cursor-move SFX -- the unambiguous 'this is a navigable menu' audio cue Aaron was looking for. Log shows 'sub_49FD50(2): pCurrentDialogSlot 0xFF -> 0x02' confirming the address resolved and was written. Files changed: src/dialog_inject.cpp (~30 lines), src/ff8_accessibility.h (this version), CHANGELOG.md (top entry, push-quality body), DEVNOTES.md, NEXT_SESSION_PROMPT.md.
  // v0.15.5.1: Fix Phase 2a PARTIAL outcome from v0.15.5 BAT. v0.15.5 BAT confirmed Phase 1 still works perfectly (F12 -> opcode_mes returns 3, slot 1 trans 0->0x400->0x1000, gameObj.D3=D4=0x02, FieldDialog hook spoke the elevator dialog), but Phase 2a (Shift+F12 -> opcode_ask) returned 1 with slot 2 entirely untouched: trans=0x0000 vel=0x0000 state=0x0 field16=0x00, gameObj.D2=0x00 across all 28 polls, slot+0x29 firstQ=0xFF and +0x2A lastQ=0xFF (uninitialized). Diagnosis from extending the disassembly walk through 0x52956D-0x5296B6: opcode_ask checks two persistent script_context bytes ctx[+0x174] ("current pending ASK slot" tracker) and ctx[+0x175] ("ASK pending bitmask") via test al, dl where al=ctx[+0x175] and dl=1<<ctx[+0x174]. If the test result is zero (i.e., ctx[+0x175] doesn't have the bit at position ctx[+0x174] set), the je 0x529622 branches AWAY from the .alloc path that would call set_window_object_ASK. Instead it lands at the answer-correlation path which checks word [esi+0x204]: if 0 (initial), takes a side path at 0x529683 that calls sub_49FD50 / sub_49FD70 / sub_4A0660 (the third just sets slot.velocity to 0xFE00, none call SWO_ASK), increments [esi+0x204] to 1, and returns 1. That's exactly what v0.15.5 hit. The natural FF8 script-VM sets ctx[+0x174]/[+0x175] via a preparatory opcode before opcode_ask runs; our injected call skipped that opcode. v0.15.5.1 fix: add s_phantomCtx[0x174] = 0 and s_phantomCtx[0x175] = 1 BEFORE writing the script-stack args. With these set, cl=0, al=1, edx=1<<0=1, test al, dl = 1 & 1 = 1 (non-zero), je is NOT taken, execution falls through to the slot-busy check at 0x529588 (gameObj.D2 & (1<<slot)), then -- if D2 bit for our slot is clear (which v0.15.5 PRE confirmed for slot 2: D2=0x00) -- to .alloc at 0x5295AB. .alloc calls field_get_dialog_string for msg 0 of the current field, calls set_window_object_ASK(slot, text_ptr, arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5) with our four script-stack values, sets gameObj.D2 |= (1<<slot) at 0x529613, and returns 1. The slot is now populated with the elevator ASK text and the cursor range, and the engine renders it on subsequent frames. Implementation surface: ~30 lines added in dialog_inject.cpp (the two ctx-byte writes plus a documentation block explaining the 0x52956D-0x529582 test mechanic and a new log line confirming the values were set). NO changes to dialog_inject.h, dinput8.cpp, or any other file. Predicted v0.15.5.1 BAT outcome (replays Phase 2a in doani1_2): ret=1, slot 2 trans advances 0 -> 0x400 -> 0x1000 (matching Phase 1 MES pattern), gameObj.D2 acquires bit 2 (0x04) post-call, slot+0x29 firstQ and slot+0x2A lastQ acquire values from our four script-stack args (1/3/2/2 in some order), the existing FieldDialog [ASK] hook fires and SAPI speaks the elevator dialog with parsed choices, and the dialog renders visually. F11 screenshot post-fire confirms render. If SUCCESS: empirical map of which arg lands in slot+0x29/0x2A/0x2C is logged for v0.15.6 Phase 2b (custom text + answer detection + chase wiring). If still PARTIAL: the slot got populated but cursor doesn't track input, indicating the engine's input handler needs additional state we haven't mirrored (suspect: an entry in the ASK pending list elsewhere, or a slot-state byte not in our model). Both outcomes leave the empirical SWO_ASK arg map in the log either way -- the slot+0x29/0x2A/0x2C decode runs even on partial, so we learn something. Risk: very low. The two ctx bytes are persistent script_context state which the natural FF8 script-VM writes anyway during ASK preparation; we're just preempting that write with values matching what would naturally land there. The phantom ctx is still our private buffer, not FF8's real script_context, so no engine state is being overwritten externally. Files changed: src/dialog_inject.cpp (~30 lines), src/ff8_accessibility.h (this version), CHANGELOG.md (top entry, push-quality body), DEVNOTES.md, NEXT_SESSION_PROMPT.md.
  // v0.15.5: Phase 2a -- experimental opcode_ask call. v0.15.4 BAT was complete success: the F12 fire of opcode_mes(&phantom_ctx) in field doani1_2 produced ret=3, the existing dialog hook spoke the field's msg 0 ("Selphie / Wanna go up? / Go up / Stay"), the slot poll showed +0x1C advancing 0 -> 0x400 (+15ms) -> 0x1000 (+125ms) and held, the state machine progressed 0 -> 1 -> 7, gameObj.D3/D4 bits set for slot 1, show_dialog callback fired for slot 1, and the F11 screenshot at 17:36:00 confirmed the dialog visually rendered indistinguishable from any natural FF8 MES. Recipe is unambiguously proven. Useful incidental finding: dispatch table opcode_mes value (0x649E57F0) differed from the cached value (0x00528F20) -- FFNx wraps these table entries; the defensive table-with-cached-fallback pattern correctly chained through FFNx. v0.15.5 ships Phase 2a: same recipe extended to opcode_ask. Adds Phase2_TestAsk to dialog_inject.cpp/.h, bound to Shift+F12 (Phase 1 stays on F12 alone per the F12 rule of one diagnostic per physical key state). Phantom script_context with SP=6 (opcode_ask pulls 6 args off the script-VM stack vs opcode_mes's 2). Stack layout from disassembly walk of opcode_ask body 0x00529520-0x005295D7: stack[SP-5] = slot index (CONFIRMED via the assertion check at 0x52955A: cmp edi, eax; jl .ok), stack[SP-4] = msg_id (CONFIRMED via mov eax, [esp+0x18] then push eax; call field_get_dialog_string at 0x5295CD), stack[SP-3] -> SWO_ASK arg2 (clamp lower bound), stack[SP-2] -> SWO_ASK arg3 (clamp upper bound, also written to slot+0x29 firstQ), stack[SP-1] -> SWO_ASK arg4 (clamped value, written to slot+0x2A lastQ), stack[SP] -> SWO_ASK arg5 (aux byte at slot+0x2B in slot-indexed aux table). Phase 2a target: slot 2 (avoids Phase 1's slot 1 to prevent gameObj.D2 collision -- the slot-busy gate at 0x529588-0x52959E rejects with ret=5 if (1<<slot) bit already set). msg_id = 0 (every field has msg 0; in Aaron's BAT field doani1_2 msg 0 is the Selphie elevator ASK with